.sp
The file\-writing tools (\fBconvert\fP, \fBwrite_table\fP, \fBedit_table\fP,
\fBtransform_columns\fP, \fBanonymize\fP) are dropped under \fB\-\-mcp\-read\-only\fP.
.sp
The defaults (response row cap of 1000 rows, per\-cell byte cap of 64 KiB,
and file\-loader cap of 5,000,000 rows) are configurable under Octa\(cqs
Settings → MCP and Settings → Performance. They are read once at
server startup; changes require a restart. Per\-call, pass \fBlimit: 0\fP
to lift the response cap and \fBunlimited: true\fP to lift the file\-loader
cap so the tool sees every row on disk. Parquet files with very many
row groups fall back to a DuckDB\-backed reader automatically.
